id: violent-mental-state
name: Violent Mental State
order: 2
category: mind
importance: primary
description: >
  Savage and nearly feral, Creatures are prone to instinctual or emotional decisions instead of rational ones.
text: >
  Violent Mental State (Mind): Savage and nearly feral, Creatures are prone to instinctual or emotional decisions instead of rational ones.
  (1)-[Passive]: Increase your Wound Rolls by 2(T) while in the Raging, Surging, or Feral State.
  (2)-[Triggered/Start of Turn, 1/Encounter]: If you are below the Injured Health Threshold, enter the Surging State until the end of your next turn.
  (3)-[Triggered/Power, 1/Encounter]: Enter the Feral State until the end of the Combat Encounter.

---

[passive]
# (1)
if (inState("raging") || inState("surging") || inState("feral")) {
    wound += 2(T);
}

# (2) Your turn begins, Injured or worse: Surging till the end of your next turn. Automatic by default, its Triggered/Automatic button.
[triggered/start-of-turn, 1/encounter, effect 2]
requires belowThreshold("injured");
enterState(surging, 1, next-turn);

# (3) The Power Up used: Feral till the Combat Encounter ends. Ticked in its window.
[triggered/power, 1/encounter, effect 3]
enterState(feral, 1, encounter);
